To start i need to upgrade my current ceaser cipher. fixing some main glaring problems like:

- the code does not wrap around the alphabet, causing letters like z to go into characters. this can be fixed by simply laying out the alphabet in a string variable, and the same for the capitals of those letters (just use .upper). then, inside a for loop for each letter in the message entered by the user, ill have an if statement check if the letters in the message entered by the user is in the alphabet or upper alphabet, if so, the code will l=move each letter up the alphabet by the key. if we use modulo 26 on this equation, it will return us back around to the beginning of the alphabet if we exceed 25. for example, since we're programming the alphabet starts at 0 not 1, so a is 0. this means z, the last letter, is 25. if the key is 3 this pushes it to position 28, which if we then % by 26, takes us back to 2. this doees mean however that spaces, punctuation and numbers will not be shifted in the message. it does mean that uppercase remains uppdercase and lowercase remains lowercase.

